  "conclusion": "v8 fixes the source-delivery gate for these four artifacts: all complete sources are accepted, including safe literal helper defaults, with no line-count rejection. It does not establish a usable program branch: all four native plan validations reject and no prediction or action executes. Zero-action feedback faithfully delivers the actual first plan-validation error and full source once, but neither follow-up yields an accepted plan. ft09 actually abstains after caught string-index errors, and su15 follow-up abstains after selecting background as its target and finding no candidate. Relaxing metadata/evidence gates would not turn these abstentions into useful actions.",
  "failure_analysis": {
    "ft09": "Both unmodified programs treat frame.ascii (native str) as a two-dimensional row container. First _legend line25 and second _cell_layout line5 raise IndexError, caught by plan_program; returned status=abstain/actions=[]/replaces=[]/evidence_pixels=[]. Online reports the first schema error about empty replaces and does not expose the handled root cause. The feedback revision retains the same API mistake.",
    "su15_first": "This source parses ASCII correctly and returns ready MOUSE(61,30), but _target reads uppercase B background runs as a pocket and chooses (62,31), contradicting its own prose about lowercase b rows11–19. Evidence has13 records,2 duplicate coordinates,6 wrong S claims. Duplicate is actual first online error. An unreached offline predictor also fails exact declared projection coverage.",
    "su15_retry": "The duplicate-evidence feedback leads to a new piece search with safe literal defaults, but target remains background(62,31); no component anchor is knight-connected under its pixel-distance rule. Actual return is abstain/actions=[]/evidence=[]/replaces=[route]. Nonempty-evidence rejection does not mean a useful ready plan was withheld.",
    "representation": "All four artifacts ignore the already supplied frame.object_evidence helper. ft09 uses assumed board constants and su15 synthesizes its own background run/anchor representation. No real action exists to verify selected roles, object-footprint completeness, dynamics or target correctness."
  },
  "feedback_assessment": {
    "delivery_integrity": "Both retries receive the actual host first error, actual before=after identity, complete failed source exactly once in the compact request package, same live facts and dependency code; old prose omitted explicitly with hashes retained.",
    "static_aggregate_online": "No static source rejection occurs, so aggregate static diagnostics have no online error case in v8. This run validates acceptance of these sources, not effectiveness of aggregate diagnostics.",
